Building and installing the Linux VLM
====================================

Requirements: x86_64 Linux, GCC, CMake 3.20 or newer, Make or Ninja, pthreads,
libm, libdl, and development headers/libraries for X11, Xlib-xcb, and libcrypt.
CLISP is needed only when regenerating the interpreter sources.

Configure, build, and test:

    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build --parallel
    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

For Ninja, add -G Ninja to the first command in a new build directory.
In-source builds are not supported. The executables are build/src/genera and
build/src/byteswap_world. Their command-line arguments have not changed.
With a multi-configuration generator, build with --config Release and pass
-C Release to ctest; executables are then in build/src/Release.

Install the two executables (default prefix /usr/local):

    cmake --install build

Choose another prefix with -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/desired/path at configure
time, or cmake --install build --prefix /desired/path. Installation may require
privileges if the destination is not writable. World images, debugger images,
and Lisp patches are separate runtime resources and are not installed.

Configuration options (pass -DNAME=VALUE to cmake -S . -B build):

    CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE          Release (default), Debug, RelWithDebInfo,
                             or MinSizeRel for single-configuration generators
    BUILD_TESTING            ON by default; builds the floating-point test
    VLM_FAST                 ON: -Ofast in Release/RelWithDebInfo; OFF: -O2
    VLM_NATIVE               ON: -march=native; OFF: generic x86_64 code
    VLM_AUTOSTART            ON: boot the Genera world automatically
    VLM_USE_TAP              ON: TAP networking; OFF: TUN networking
    VLM_DEBUG_DISK           OFF: disk debugging
    VLM_DEBUG_NETWORK        OFF: network debugging
    VLM_DEBUG_NETWORK_IP     OFF: IP packet debugging
    VLM_DEBUG_NETWORK_CHAOS  OFF: Chaos packet debugging
    VLM_DEBUG_NETWORK_ARP    OFF: ARP packet debugging
    VLM_DEBUG_NETWORK_ICMP   OFF: ICMP packet debugging (also enables IP)
    VLM_REGENERATE_STUBS     OFF: use checked-in interpreter C sources
    CLISP_EXECUTABLE         CLISP path, detected when regeneration is enabled

Protocol debugging requires VLM_DEBUG_NETWORK=ON. Debug builds use CMake's
normal debug flags; VLM_FAST affects only Release and RelWithDebInfo.
VLM_NATIVE=OFF is useful when distributing binaries to other x86_64 machines.
GNU C99 and -fno-strict-aliasing are required by the existing emulator code.

To develop the interpreter's assembler or Lisp macros:

    cmake -S . -B build -DVLM_REGENERATE_STUBS=ON
    cmake --build build --parallel

CMake runs CLISP when the inputs change and puts generated instruction sources
in build/stub, without modifying the checked-in copies. To generate without
compiling, use cmake --build build --target generate-stubs.

Optional runtime integration test (requires Python 3, an X display, a free
configured TAP interface, and the world/debugger files):

    python3 tests/shutdown.py -- ./build/src/genera <your usual arguments>

This test starts and stops four temporary instances, so stop any instance
using that TAP before running it. It is separate from ctest, which does not
need a world, display, or network device.
